%% One question through /ask. The companion component.mmd shows the structure.
%%
%% Two things worth reading off this: the refusals happen before any inference,
%% and the model is called two to four times — once per planning step, once to
%% draft, once more only if the guard finds something. That call count is where
%% the latency lives, which is why FD_REASONING_EFFORT is a documented dial.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant API as filingdesk · agent.py
    participant MCP as mcp_server · stdio
    participant DUCK as filings.duckdb
    participant VEC as vault.db
    participant LLM as model endpoint

    U->>API: POST /api/report · question + ticker

    alt no model configured
        API-->>U: dashboard-only refusal, stated not warned
    end

    API->>API: policy.check_scope — regex, no inference
    alt advice · market data · forecast
        API-->>U: typed refusal, model never consulted
    end

    API->>API: companies.resolve(ticker)
    alt not an SEC registrant
        API-->>U: unknown_ticker + closest matches
    end

    API->>MCP: spawn subprocess, list_tools

    loop planning · up to 4 steps
        API->>LLM: chat with tool schemas (effort: FD_PLAN_REASONING_EFFORT)
        LLM-->>API: tool_calls, or none to finish
        API->>API: toolcall.validate — schema, ticker, arguments
        alt rejected
            API->>LLM: rejection reason, retry (max 3)
        end
        API->>MCP: fd_get_concept · fd_compute_metric · fd_list_concepts
        MCP->>DUCK: SQL over normalised facts
        DUCK-->>MCP: rows
        MCP->>MCP: series.py dedupe · derive Q4 · metrics.py ratios
        MCP-->>API: typed facts with accession numbers
    end

    alt no facts retrieved
        API-->>U: refusal naming which of the four reasons applied
    end

    opt notes vault configured and embeddings available
        API->>LLM: embed question
        API->>VEC: cosine top-k
        VEC-->>API: passages — framing only, no figures
    end

    API->>LLM: draft, every figure needing a fact marker
    LLM-->>API: draft markdown

    API->>API: guard.check — each numeral vs retrieved values
    opt untraceable figure found
        API->>LLM: repair, offending claims listed
        LLM-->>API: corrected draft
        API->>API: re-check, once only
    end

    alt clean
        API-->>U: answer + fact table + accession numbers + trace_id
    else still unsupported
        API-->>U: same, with the offending figures struck and listed
    end
